{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Therefore, on the day I arise</b> — the rising will be eternal. Rabbi Moses said: to destroy the world, like <i>בבקר יאכל עד</i> (it shall eat until morning). And he said: <i>כי לעד</i> — the act, like <i>לרד לפניו גוים</i> (to go down before Him, nations)." "<b>My judgment</b> — it is a judgment that I shall do thus." "<b>And the meaning of My jealousy</b> — because they worshipped other gods, in the manner of <i>El kanna</i> (a jealous God), for this is future. And according to Rabbi Moses' opinion: concerning the Second Temple, they will turn to worship HaShem alone with a pure language — this is the Holy Tongue [Hebrew], by which alone the revered Name is called."], :book :zephaniah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :register {:flags {2 ["God"]}}, :notes {0 "Rabbi Moses reads לעד as 'destruction' (from ע-ו-ד 'to set/destroy'), while Ibn Ezra reads it as 'eternity' (from ע-ד 'perpetuity'). The second citation is from 2 Samuel 22:48."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zephaniah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zfanya"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:47:29.287386281Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}